{"name":"Herb Robert","hex":"#dda0df","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"herb robert","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of herb Robert."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/herb_robert"}],"entries":[{"title":"Geranium robertianum","blocks":[{"text":"Geranium robertianum, commonly known as herb-robert or, in North America, as Robert's geranium, is a species of cranesbill that is widespread throughout the northern hemisphere and introduced to some countries in the southern. It is common in woods, hedges, gardens, and on waste ground, and can also be found on shingle beaches and limestone pavements. It is not rare or threatened and in some places it is considered to be invasive."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Herb-Robert_800.jpg/330px-Herb-Robert_800.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geranium_robertianum","wikidata":"Q160096"},{"title":"Herb","blocks":[{"text":"Herbs are a widely distributed and widespread group of plants, excluding vegetables, with savory or aromatic properties that are used for flavoring and garnishing food, for medicinal purposes, or for fragrances. Culinary use typically distinguishes herbs from spices. Herbs generally refers to the leafy green or flowering parts of a plant, while spices are usually dried and produced from other parts of the plant, including seeds, bark, roots and fruits."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Garden_of_herbs.jpg/330px-Garden_of_herbs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herb","wikidata":"Q207123"},{"title":"Robert","blocks":[{"text":"The name Robert is an ancient Germanic given name, from Proto-Germanic *Hrōþi- \"fame\" and *berhta- \"bright\" (Hrōþiberhtaz). Compare Old Dutch Robrecht and Old High German Hrodebert. It is the second most frequently used given name of ancient Germanic origin. It is also in use as a surname. Another commonly used form of the name is Rupert."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Stirling_Castle_20080505_Robert_the_Bruce.jpg/330px-Stirling_Castle_20080505_Robert_the_Bruce.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert","wikidata":"Q4927937"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Geranium_robertianum_Duncan_Down.jpg/500px-Geranium_robertianum_Duncan_Down.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Geranium_robertianum_Duncan_Down.jpg/1280px-Geranium_robertianum_Duncan_Down.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Geranium_robertianum_Duncan_Down.jpg/500px-Geranium_robertianum_Duncan_Down.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The flower has ten stamens in two rings of five; the inner anthers open first.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeranium_robertianum_Duncan_Down.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Geranium_robertianum_leaf.jpg/500px-Geranium_robertianum_leaf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Geranium_robertianum_leaf.jpg/1280px-Geranium_robertianum_leaf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Geranium_robertianum_leaf.jpg/500px-Geranium_robertianum_leaf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The leaves are typically ternate (as here) or palmate.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeranium_robe